WEBVTT

00:00:10.928 --> 00:00:12.930
[theme music playing]

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:47.524
[thunder rumbling]

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.335
[knocking on door]

00:02:15.177 --> 00:02:18.513
[man] Master Marco.
You requested more salt cakes?

00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:20.933
Yes.
Thank you.

00:02:41.119 --> 00:02:42.955
[gatekeeper shouts in foreign language]

00:02:43.038 --> 00:02:44.790
[palace gates opening]

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.890
[men groaning]

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.948
General Aruka advised retreat.

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:22.995
I gave the order that we turn and fight...
like Mongols.

00:03:23.078 --> 00:03:24.662
[Kublai] Mongols do not lose.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.709
I have thought of nothing else

00:03:29.793 --> 00:03:32.337
these past days and nights.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.215
A ride preceded by victory
is much shorter.

00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:37.801
True words such as these
can only be drawn

00:03:37.885 --> 00:03:40.053
from a well of personal experience.

00:03:41.179 --> 00:03:42.597
Leave me with my son.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.391
Our son...

00:03:44.474 --> 00:03:46.268
is wounded.

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.229
Let me see.

00:03:49.312 --> 00:03:51.732
A scar that will always
remind me of Wuchang...

00:03:51.815 --> 00:03:54.943
and the men and horses that died there.
That is the only wound.

00:03:55.027 --> 00:03:56.737
It too will fade.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.989
[Kublai]
Empress, please.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.615
Go to the healer...

00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:04.327
Immediately.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:15.380
You will ride to Karakorum...
pay a visit to Ariq.

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:17.966
I want to know why
my brother pledged horse and bow,

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.677
but did not arrive
to support my army.

00:04:21.303 --> 00:04:22.387
A horse messenger can cover 300--

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.973
Your horse messenger...

00:04:26.308 --> 00:04:29.477
did a fine job at Wuchang.
Did he not?

00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:33.148
Did you even send
a falcon to my brother?

00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:36.026
Of course I did.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.652
[Kublai] Return to me the truth.

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:43.325
Go see the healer,
as your mother instructed.

00:04:54.502 --> 00:04:56.463
[Marco] How are the merchants taxed?

00:04:56.546 --> 00:04:58.381
They pay a fee for their stalls,

00:04:58.465 --> 00:05:01.844
and the higher fee is for more traffic,
more customers.

00:05:01.927 --> 00:05:03.345
More money, eh?

00:05:03.428 --> 00:05:05.263
Are there ever holdouts?

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:07.557
Inside the Imperial Wall?
[chuckles]

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.767
Very rare.

00:05:09.852 --> 00:05:11.519
Too good a thing they have here.

00:05:11.603 --> 00:05:13.981
These vendors know,
they cheat on tribute,

00:05:14.064 --> 00:05:16.649
they end up peddling outside the wall.

00:05:16.733 --> 00:05:19.652
[Marco] In Venice, those who do not meet
their obligations are imprisoned.

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:21.113
Is it the same here?

00:05:21.196 --> 00:05:24.574
No, no, no.
Thieves are branded thieves.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.743
Marked, they struggle.

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:29.913
Their sons beg,
their wives and daughters whore.

00:05:29.997 --> 00:05:32.207
They live off
Lady Chabi's charity loaves.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:34.667
But they live.

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.086
Sometimes.

00:05:37.462 --> 00:05:41.258
Severity of punishment...
not for me to comment on.

00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:46.513
This is for the Vice Regent Yusuf,
and the wisdom of his Secretariat.

00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:49.849
[Marco] What is this fabric?

00:05:49.933 --> 00:05:51.143
Uh, linen.

00:05:51.226 --> 00:05:53.353
These Jurchen make it in Manchuria.

00:05:53.436 --> 00:05:55.230
They don't have copper coins
to pay this month.

00:05:55.313 --> 00:05:57.315
So, I let them pay
with what they have.

00:05:57.399 --> 00:05:59.902
[speaking Mandarin]

00:06:03.821 --> 00:06:05.448
[children laughing]

00:06:07.951 --> 00:06:09.327
Hey. Hey.

00:06:09.411 --> 00:06:12.915
Can we get rid of these... pissants?

00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:14.958
These are my children.

00:06:15.042 --> 00:06:16.709
[laughs]

00:06:16.793 --> 00:06:18.336
They follow me around like I'm a king.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.088
[Marco]
King of a fine brood, sir.

00:06:20.172 --> 00:06:24.217
With my own Venetian slave, huh?
Pissants!

00:06:24.301 --> 00:06:25.427
[Sanga laughing]

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.345
I love that!

00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:33.351
[Sanga sighs]
Let me put this away.

00:06:33.435 --> 00:06:35.979
[Marco] Thank you for dinner.
It was delicious.

00:06:37.314 --> 00:06:38.648
[Sanga] Spices?

00:06:38.731 --> 00:06:41.526
You wanna talk about spices?

00:06:41.609 --> 00:06:42.735
These spiceries pay

00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:45.613
three and a third percent.

00:06:45.697 --> 00:06:47.532
From the wine they make of the rice...

00:06:48.533 --> 00:06:51.203
they generate great revenue.

00:06:51.286 --> 00:06:52.996
Thus, they must pay duty.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.083
Untold money to the Khan!

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:58.626
What is that, Sanga?

00:06:58.710 --> 00:06:59.836
Huh?

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:06.051
[speaking Persian]

00:07:09.804 --> 00:07:11.306
This, Marco...

00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:13.808
they're verses of love.

00:07:13.891 --> 00:07:16.728
See, I travel to collect.

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:17.938
So, when I travel...

00:07:18.021 --> 00:07:22.025
I leave words of love on paper
for my Goland.

00:07:22.109 --> 00:07:23.568
So she remembers
she has a husband!

00:07:24.861 --> 00:07:26.404
[Sanga chuckles]

00:07:26.488 --> 00:07:30.117
And the Silk Road?
Do we ever travel there to collect taxes?

00:07:31.576 --> 00:07:33.495
"We"? No.

00:07:33.578 --> 00:07:36.914
I travel to collect.
Once a fortnight or so.

00:07:36.999 --> 00:07:38.000
You...

00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:41.544
are not permitted
to travel outside of Cambulac.

00:07:41.628 --> 00:07:43.088
Hmm?

00:07:43.171 --> 00:07:46.049
The wonders of Khan's City is plenty.

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.175
Hmm?

00:07:47.259 --> 00:07:48.343
So, please...

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:51.554
don't speak of this again...
because I like you.

00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:53.348
My slave.

00:07:53.431 --> 00:07:54.891
<i>Salute!</i>

00:07:57.602 --> 00:07:59.271
[Sanga chuckles]

00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:06.903
[Mei Lin] Noble Tiger traveled
a great distance...

00:08:06.987 --> 00:08:09.572
and began to find
his eyes growing heavy.

00:08:10.615 --> 00:08:14.744
Noble Tiger was very sleepy, you see...

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:17.664
for he was very old.

00:08:17.747 --> 00:08:19.582
Did he have no more teeth?

00:08:19.666 --> 00:08:22.627
[laughs]
He still had teeth...

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:25.547
just no longer sharp.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:30.677
And so, Noble Tiger lay himself
under a great banyan tree...

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.555
and fell into a deep slumber.

00:08:33.638 --> 00:08:39.144
He had the most beautiful dream
of a long shady path.

00:08:39.227 --> 00:08:43.190
And as he walked down it...

00:08:43.273 --> 00:08:46.984
he grew young again
and began a life anew.

00:08:48.736 --> 00:08:51.073
So, he slept forever?

00:08:53.116 --> 00:08:55.452
Yes.

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:59.622
But all of his friends in the forest
were so happy for him.

00:08:59.706 --> 00:09:04.377
Then they remembered
all the treasures he left behind.

00:09:04.461 --> 00:09:08.048
You, Ling Ling,
are the sweetest...

00:09:08.131 --> 00:09:12.094
greatest treasure
your father ever gifted me.

00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:16.348
One I will selfishly hoard forever.

00:09:16.431 --> 00:09:18.183
Hello, Sunflower.

00:09:18.683 --> 00:09:19.851
Uncle!

00:09:20.977 --> 00:09:24.689
Uncle's most precious.
Born in the Year of the Monkey.

00:09:24.772 --> 00:09:26.191
Oh.
[giggles]

00:09:26.274 --> 00:09:29.902
That's why you're so clever.
Precious and clever.

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:31.738
Go. Show the children your new gift.

00:09:36.784 --> 00:09:38.661
The Emperor is breathing his last

00:09:38.745 --> 00:09:41.998
and he has requested
the presence of his imperial consort.

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:45.085
It is a tragedy
that the fates will not allow him

00:09:45.168 --> 00:09:48.296
the time to bear witness
to the fall of Kublai Khan.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:52.134
Perhaps the Goddess of Mercy
is sparing him a far worse vision.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:10:00.225
Men will one day sing
songs about me, sister.

00:10:00.308 --> 00:10:03.311
Jia Sidao, the prime minister
who vanquished the demon

00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:05.355
and saved the Song.

00:10:06.648 --> 00:10:09.359
I will bring my daughter
to say goodbye to her father...

00:10:10.735 --> 00:10:12.279
and to the Empire.

00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:06.374
[neighing]

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:53.338
I did not mean to startle you.

00:11:53.421 --> 00:11:56.090
-Are you following me?
-No.

00:11:56.173 --> 00:11:58.760
I saw you and approached.

00:12:02.347 --> 00:12:03.848
What are you doing out here?

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:06.934
I might ask you the same.

00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.228
There is no citizen of Cambulac

00:12:09.312 --> 00:12:11.814
foolish enough to look at,
let alone talk to me.

00:12:11.898 --> 00:12:13.400
Do you know who I am?

00:12:15.026 --> 00:12:16.861
I know only your protector.

00:12:16.944 --> 00:12:19.113
And if Za Bing were to
catch you anywhere near me...

00:12:19.196 --> 00:12:20.490
he would run you through.

00:12:22.659 --> 00:12:24.619
I trust you will not report me.

00:12:26.203 --> 00:12:27.789
[bell tolls]

00:12:30.292 --> 00:12:32.294
So... who are you?

00:12:33.836 --> 00:12:36.631
I am the Blue Princess
of the Bayaut tribe.

00:12:36.714 --> 00:12:39.967
You ride as Mongol...
not princess.

00:12:40.051 --> 00:12:43.262
All Mongol women are born
to the horse and the bow.

00:12:45.307 --> 00:12:46.349
May I assist you?

00:12:46.433 --> 00:12:48.393
No.

00:12:48.476 --> 00:12:50.102
I am simply being polite.

00:12:50.186 --> 00:12:53.315
Something a noble woman
such as yourself should be tutored in.

00:12:53.398 --> 00:12:55.567
I need not be polite
to someone like you.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.819
[scoffs] Someone like me?

00:12:57.902 --> 00:12:59.654
Someone beneath me.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:07.662
I will forgive your ignorance
in the ways of your new home.

00:13:07.745 --> 00:13:08.996
This is not my home.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.333
Many before you
have thought the same.

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:14.794
You speak from experience.

00:13:14.877 --> 00:13:17.296
Why do you imagine that?

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.216
I see behind your words.

00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:24.220
If you are the Princess of the Bayaut...
where is your Queen?

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:26.305
Your King?

00:13:27.432 --> 00:13:29.726
You're a prisoner...

00:13:29.809 --> 00:13:31.936
like me.

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:37.650
I am kept for royalty.
My future is in some distant palace.

00:13:37.734 --> 00:13:40.236
You are a slave of the Khan.

00:13:42.238 --> 00:13:44.532
I am nothing like you.

00:13:57.712 --> 00:13:59.130
[bell tolls]

00:14:01.549 --> 00:14:03.426
Try to keep up, if you can.

00:14:42.424 --> 00:14:44.133
[bell tolling]

00:15:07.532 --> 00:15:11.661
It won't be you who gets cattle-branded,
Princess.

00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:13.913
[thudding]

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.663
[growling]

00:16:03.004 --> 00:16:05.840
[Kublai]
You've been particularly busy of late.

00:16:07.509 --> 00:16:09.761
How goes your horse riding?

00:16:12.472 --> 00:16:15.224
You hold your tongue from me again? Hmm?

00:16:16.183 --> 00:16:19.020
How shall I tell of the
Mongolian pony, Sire?

00:16:19.103 --> 00:16:21.689
He is a fine and hardy breed.

00:16:21.773 --> 00:16:27.278
Unlike some steeds in Europe...
he needs not rest nor... coddling.

00:16:27.361 --> 00:16:28.988
Good.

00:16:29.071 --> 00:16:31.824
Because you ride to Karakorum today
with my son Jingim.

00:16:31.908 --> 00:16:35.537
Bring me back a report,
with fresh eyes.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:36.996
Let me see, Latin...

00:16:37.914 --> 00:16:40.542
the way things truly are
in the kingdom of my brother.

00:16:41.458 --> 00:16:43.335
By your will, Sire.

00:16:47.632 --> 00:16:49.133
[men urging horses]

00:17:51.528 --> 00:17:52.655
My nephew.

00:17:52.739 --> 00:17:54.031
Uncle.

00:17:55.241 --> 00:17:57.910
[Ariq] I'm honored
that my older brother has sent you.

00:17:57.994 --> 00:17:59.621
We will kill a sheep...

00:17:59.704 --> 00:18:00.830
and drink airag.

00:18:00.913 --> 00:18:02.582
Come.

00:18:09.088 --> 00:18:11.966
[Jingim] You're in the heartland
of Lord Genghis now.

00:18:12.049 --> 00:18:17.346
Beware, Polo.
Your words can get you killed.

00:18:17.429 --> 00:18:19.390
Wait out here.

00:18:25.562 --> 00:18:28.274
[Ariq] This one they call
the "Cricket Minister..."

00:18:28.357 --> 00:18:31.235
how many soldiers did he
have lying in wait at Wuchang?

00:18:31.318 --> 00:18:32.945
Not enough to defeat a Mongol army...

00:18:33.029 --> 00:18:36.032
had our reinforcements arrived.

00:18:36.115 --> 00:18:37.742
You did not attack without me?

00:18:37.825 --> 00:18:39.994
I was almost killed!

00:18:40.077 --> 00:18:43.790
My general, Aruka,
has passed to the Blue Sky!

00:18:43.873 --> 00:18:46.292
The rains cut off passage
of the Blue Horde.

00:18:46.375 --> 00:18:47.627
You should have sent word.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:49.879
I did.

00:18:49.962 --> 00:18:53.049
My best rider... Duwa.

00:18:53.132 --> 00:18:55.592
They captured him outside of Wuchang.

00:18:55.677 --> 00:18:58.137
Tied his head to his horse...

00:18:58.220 --> 00:18:59.847
let it run home.

00:18:59.931 --> 00:19:02.558
Right to his <i>ger...</i>

00:19:02.642 --> 00:19:04.185
and his children.

00:19:15.404 --> 00:19:17.239
[men grunting]

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:30.712
[sheep bleating]

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:36.843
May I see?

00:19:38.427 --> 00:19:40.096
[horse neighing]

00:19:43.015 --> 00:19:46.143
They are... magnificent beasts.

00:20:08.415 --> 00:20:11.711
When you were a child,
I called you Altai.

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:18.592
After the mountains me
and your father hunted as boys.

00:20:18.675 --> 00:20:22.972
Kublai insisted on a Chinese name.
Jingim.

00:20:26.517 --> 00:20:28.770
Remind me of its meaning.

00:20:29.771 --> 00:20:30.772
Golden.

00:20:31.939 --> 00:20:33.024
Golden.

00:20:34.233 --> 00:20:36.527
You are his golden one, nephew.

00:20:37.528 --> 00:20:42.033
One day, they may call you...
"Jingim Khan."

00:20:43.617 --> 00:20:44.869
But beware...

00:20:46.287 --> 00:20:50.624
my big brother
is too trusting of outsiders.

00:20:50.707 --> 00:20:54.503
Persians...
and Chinese...

00:20:54.586 --> 00:20:56.798
and all kinds of religions.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.051
You and me...

00:21:00.134 --> 00:21:04.055
our blood is the wolf and the deer.

00:21:04.138 --> 00:21:07.975
Open the gates to outsiders...
secrets will they spill.

00:21:16.108 --> 00:21:18.986
Who is the Christian
who rides with you?

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:05.616
My uncle's troops were cut off
by the spring rains...

00:22:05.699 --> 00:22:07.326
east of Volga.

00:22:07.409 --> 00:22:08.577
He sent a horse messenger...

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:10.496
but the rebels intercepted.

00:22:14.291 --> 00:22:16.085
Where is the Latin?

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:19.881
[Marco] Sire?

00:22:25.970 --> 00:22:28.139
What was your impression
of the Old Capital?

00:22:29.974 --> 00:22:32.559
I found the Great Khan's brother
to be a gracious host,

00:22:32.643 --> 00:22:34.228
as Prince Jingim reported.

00:22:37.314 --> 00:22:38.399
Four wives, yes?

00:22:38.482 --> 00:22:42.694
Five.
He also keeps a large harem...

00:22:42.778 --> 00:22:44.280
quite young.

00:22:45.739 --> 00:22:47.408
But not as vast as mine.

00:22:47.491 --> 00:22:49.868
And nowhere near as charming.

00:22:49.952 --> 00:22:51.828
Certainly no girls from Kungurat.

00:22:51.913 --> 00:22:53.705
[court laughing]

00:22:57.919 --> 00:23:01.588
I have seen my uncle's army, Father.

00:23:01.672 --> 00:23:02.965
They are ready.

00:23:03.465 --> 00:23:06.635
Ariq is prepared to join
our attack on Xiangyang.

00:23:06.718 --> 00:23:09.972
This will not be another Wuchang.

00:23:10.056 --> 00:23:11.515
[court murmuring]

00:23:16.062 --> 00:23:18.981
I fear Ariq's horses
will never reach Xiangyang.

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:25.988
Speak.

00:23:28.824 --> 00:23:31.577
Ariq's horses are
in the many thousands, true.

00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:33.704
Quite fit.

00:23:33.787 --> 00:23:37.416
But how many days' ride is it from
the Old Capital to the Walled City?

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.087
Three weeks.
By desert.

00:23:46.508 --> 00:23:48.844
As the son of a merchant...

00:23:48.927 --> 00:23:52.389
they do not have the grain supplies
to move that many horses to Xiangyang.

00:23:53.307 --> 00:23:57.103
The desert alone would
cut their numbers in half.

00:23:57.186 --> 00:24:01.482
My son, Jingim, just stated that
they are ready to ride into battle.

00:24:01.565 --> 00:24:04.693
They are ready, yes, Great Khan.

00:24:04.776 --> 00:24:07.654
But only if that battle
was closer to home.

00:24:09.991 --> 00:24:11.575
[Jingim] Do you accuse my uncle,

00:24:11.658 --> 00:24:13.785
brother to the Khan, of treason?

00:24:14.703 --> 00:24:18.290
I only describe what I see,
as I saw it.

00:24:32.638 --> 00:24:34.640
Yusuf...

00:24:34.723 --> 00:24:38.269
dispatch a night rider
to verify the Latin's report.

00:24:53.659 --> 00:24:54.910
[door closes]

00:25:01.833 --> 00:25:06.130
You will not be gaining favors
by your charming stories anymore.

00:25:07.714 --> 00:25:09.508
Not without a tongue.

00:25:53.219 --> 00:25:55.262
The sword you hid is weak.

00:25:55.346 --> 00:25:58.724
Your water won't last you two days.

00:25:58.807 --> 00:26:01.977
But the salt cakes were... delicious.

00:26:05.606 --> 00:26:07.774
I called Ariq a liar tonight.

00:26:07.858 --> 00:26:10.944
That was foolish.
Were your words true?

00:26:11.027 --> 00:26:12.654
Yes.

00:26:12.738 --> 00:26:14.823
Run now, they will find you.

00:26:14.906 --> 00:26:16.450
Stay...

00:26:16.533 --> 00:26:20.036
I can train you to survive in whatever
world you choose to make your home.

00:26:20.121 --> 00:26:22.080
This is not my home.

00:26:22.164 --> 00:26:23.749
[Hundred Eyes] I understand.

00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:27.294
Where did the Khan get you from?

00:26:28.754 --> 00:26:30.214
I said I would train you...

00:26:31.173 --> 00:26:35.093
not wallow in nostalgia with you.

00:26:59.910 --> 00:27:01.662
[grunting]

00:27:33.194 --> 00:27:35.070
[Marco panting]

00:27:36.363 --> 00:27:38.699
Why do you think the
sword has a colored sash?

00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:41.034
To look pretty?

00:27:53.255 --> 00:27:55.882
[Jingim] He's advanced quickly
to the broadsword.

00:27:58.677 --> 00:28:00.512
You schooled him well, Hundred Eyes.

00:28:02.013 --> 00:28:05.434
May I interrupt
the student's training for a word?

00:28:05.517 --> 00:28:08.562
You're the Prince.
You may kill him, if that's your desire.

00:28:09.855 --> 00:28:10.856
[drawing sword]

00:28:18.822 --> 00:28:22.701
Humiliate me
in front of the court again...

00:28:22.784 --> 00:28:24.536
I will kill you.

00:28:34.546 --> 00:28:35.881
You were right.

00:28:37.633 --> 00:28:39.218
Ariq betrayed us.

00:28:54.525 --> 00:28:58.194
Ariq sends me a treacherous gift.

00:28:58.279 --> 00:29:01.865
He remembers how much
I love the king of the hunters.

00:29:01.948 --> 00:29:05.577
Ariq is a dog,
that would eat its own afterbirth.

00:29:05.661 --> 00:29:07.288
[Kublai chuckles]

00:29:07.371 --> 00:29:11.625
He has always believed that he
should be Khan of Khans. Not you.

00:29:13.752 --> 00:29:16.380
Before the sun sets today...

00:29:16.463 --> 00:29:19.675
I will close down the Gobi trade routes...

00:29:19.758 --> 00:29:22.553
starve Karakorum.

00:29:22.636 --> 00:29:26.265
My younger brother will have
no place to go but Siberia.

00:29:26.348 --> 00:29:29.100
So forgiving, Great Kublai.

00:29:29.184 --> 00:29:34.273
You slaughter entire cities,
yet you allow Ariq to run to Siberia.

00:29:34.356 --> 00:29:35.941
I know how to punish my brother.

00:29:36.024 --> 00:29:38.151
He almost killed your son.

00:29:39.736 --> 00:29:42.739
Ariq believes he can pleasure
your women better than you.

00:29:42.823 --> 00:29:43.990
[Kublai chuckles]

00:29:44.074 --> 00:29:45.951
Does that excite you, Empress?

00:29:46.034 --> 00:29:49.871
Ariq should be trampled
by 1,000 horses

00:29:49.955 --> 00:29:52.499
and left on a steppe to rot.

00:29:56.044 --> 00:29:59.673
That... would excite me.

00:30:17.941 --> 00:30:19.150
[crickets chirping]

00:30:37.586 --> 00:30:39.170
[Governor] Ariq Khan?

00:30:39.254 --> 00:30:40.714
[Jia Sidao]
Kublai's younger brother in the north.

00:30:40.797 --> 00:30:44.468
We are minting his own currency
for when he is elected Khan of Khans

00:30:44.551 --> 00:30:46.928
and opens the Silk Road for the Song.

00:30:47.012 --> 00:30:49.431
Of course, I need the support
of our region's governors.

00:30:54.185 --> 00:30:56.855
You have my stamp, Sidao.

00:30:59.358 --> 00:31:02.694
And my command over the Council.

00:31:20.336 --> 00:31:22.297
[women sobbing]

00:31:22.381 --> 00:31:25.634
Men grow old,
pearls turn yellow...

00:31:25.717 --> 00:31:27.969
there is no cure.

00:31:28.053 --> 00:31:30.221
My condolences, Empress Xie.

00:31:31.264 --> 00:31:35.310
Eventually, we all
become white ashes, Sidao.

00:31:35.394 --> 00:31:38.939
But my husband has left a son.

00:31:39.022 --> 00:31:42.484
Bow to your new Emperor, Zhao Xian.

00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:49.032
[sighing]

00:31:52.160 --> 00:31:55.706
With sad news, Empress,
also comes good.

00:31:55.789 --> 00:31:58.959
We drove the Mongols
back from Wuchang.

00:31:59.042 --> 00:32:01.002
The barbarians know your Chancellor

00:32:01.086 --> 00:32:04.840
will never surrender the last
stronghold of the Song dynasty.

00:32:05.507 --> 00:32:08.760
But they will be back.
We can count on that.

00:32:08.844 --> 00:32:12.138
I fear you do count on it, Sidao.

00:32:12.222 --> 00:32:14.850
I fear you thirst for it.

00:32:14.933 --> 00:32:16.560
[loud clattering]

00:32:45.464 --> 00:32:46.715
Have you reported all?

00:32:46.798 --> 00:32:49.468
Yes, Good Minister Ahmad. Yes.

00:32:51.678 --> 00:32:53.138
You are dismissed, Sanga.

00:32:56.933 --> 00:32:58.226
Master Marco.

00:32:59.185 --> 00:33:02.648
Come. Stay.

00:33:02.731 --> 00:33:05.316
Goodbye, my Venetian slave.

00:33:05.400 --> 00:33:07.528
<i>Schiavo.</i> Huh?
[chuckles]

00:33:09.070 --> 00:33:10.238
[Ahmad] So...

00:33:10.321 --> 00:33:12.448
what is this gift I hear of?

00:33:12.533 --> 00:33:16.077
The foreign messenger
who can paint pictures with his words.

00:33:16.161 --> 00:33:19.330
How would you describe
the manner in which...

00:33:19.414 --> 00:33:20.749
the Uighurs pay their taxes?

00:33:21.708 --> 00:33:25.170
Always there's a form of ceremony.

00:33:25.253 --> 00:33:27.756
On their knees...

00:33:27.839 --> 00:33:31.342
a humble offering,
more as to a god than to a king.

00:33:31.426 --> 00:33:33.261
And the Jurchens?

00:33:33.344 --> 00:33:35.764
[Marco] Clever, and a resourceful people.

00:33:35.847 --> 00:33:39.643
Paying with the work of their hands
when they do not have the coins.

00:33:39.726 --> 00:33:42.938
[Ahmad] Masters of making linen,
I understand.

00:33:43.021 --> 00:33:45.273
So if the Jurchens
have been paying in linen,

00:33:45.356 --> 00:33:48.068
why hasn't Sanga
deposited any such tribute?

00:33:51.487 --> 00:33:54.783
I did not say
that Sanga collected such linens.

00:33:54.866 --> 00:33:59.245
Only that the Jurchens are a clever
and resourceful people.

00:34:00.956 --> 00:34:03.124
You are not the first foreigner...

00:34:03.208 --> 00:34:06.211
who has had to learn
to subsist in this kingdom.

00:34:06.294 --> 00:34:09.172
I found my way here as a child...

00:34:09.255 --> 00:34:12.801
raised in the household
of the Great Khan.

00:34:12.884 --> 00:34:17.513
So I know his heart,
and I have his trust.

00:34:17.598 --> 00:34:22.227
A lie is...
like an assault on his person, but...

00:34:22.310 --> 00:34:25.396
an honest word?
That is like a shield.

00:34:26.690 --> 00:34:28.859
So I must ask you again.

00:34:28.942 --> 00:34:30.276
Did the Jurchens...

00:34:30.360 --> 00:34:35.406
at any time...
pay their taxes in the form of linen?

00:34:37.450 --> 00:34:39.953
Perhaps Sanga simply forgot.

00:34:42.914 --> 00:34:44.750
Indeed.

00:34:58.054 --> 00:35:01.642
[singing in Mandarin]

00:35:22.495 --> 00:35:25.666
[Mei Lin speaking English]
Ling Ling... Ling Ling, go with Jing Fei.

00:35:27.751 --> 00:35:29.795
Come on. Good girl.

00:35:32.422 --> 00:35:35.091
I will see you very soon, my daughter.

00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.934
My Emperor is dead...

00:35:45.351 --> 00:35:48.313
but I am still an imperial consort.

00:35:52.859 --> 00:35:55.236
I do not bed soldiers.

00:35:55.320 --> 00:35:58.865
Chancellor Jia Sidao
has granted us permission.

00:36:24.725 --> 00:36:28.103
Two Eels, One Cave.

00:36:33.942 --> 00:36:35.610
[soldiers chuckling]

00:36:36.652 --> 00:36:38.905
Do you know this forbidden game?

00:36:39.865 --> 00:36:41.366
[soldiers speaking indistinctly]

00:37:17.193 --> 00:37:18.361
[gurgling]

00:37:19.946 --> 00:37:21.697
[soldiers shouting]

00:37:22.407 --> 00:37:23.533
[soldiers grunting]

00:37:52.728 --> 00:37:56.775
[guards shouting in Cantonese]

00:37:56.858 --> 00:37:58.443
[footsteps approaching]

00:38:06.284 --> 00:38:10.163
You should be tied to a post and
have your skin sliced from your body.

00:38:10.246 --> 00:38:13.124
I have bartered
for your political advantage.

00:38:13.208 --> 00:38:15.961
I will not barter
for the loyalty of your soldiers.

00:38:16.044 --> 00:38:17.253
[Jia Sidao] It is beneath you...

00:38:17.337 --> 00:38:18.713
I know.

00:38:20.298 --> 00:38:22.425
You will travel to Cambulac as defector.

00:38:23.384 --> 00:38:24.677
They will take you in,

00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:26.847
and just as you won
the favor of the Emperor of China...

00:38:26.930 --> 00:38:29.640
you will win the favor
of the Devil himself.

00:38:29.724 --> 00:38:31.601
Report to me.

00:38:31.684 --> 00:38:34.354
Everything he says, everything he does,
everything he dreams.

00:38:34.437 --> 00:38:36.147
[children laughing]

00:38:41.069 --> 00:38:42.445
Do not worry, sister.

00:38:42.946 --> 00:38:44.405
While you are away...

00:38:44.489 --> 00:38:47.533
I will personally care for my Sunflower.

00:38:48.493 --> 00:38:49.911
I am your blood.

00:38:49.995 --> 00:38:52.122
We give our blood for the dynasty.

00:38:52.914 --> 00:38:55.917
Your men...
they laugh at you.

00:38:56.001 --> 00:38:58.169
They call you the "Cricket Minister."

00:39:09.055 --> 00:39:11.266
[Marco] I was summoned.

00:39:11.349 --> 00:39:12.433
[Jingim] Quiet.

00:39:15.395 --> 00:39:16.771
You may begin.

00:39:17.939 --> 00:39:21.192
[shouting in Mongolian]

00:39:28.909 --> 00:39:32.370
The tax collector's deposits
did not match.

00:39:32.453 --> 00:39:33.538
What?

00:39:36.499 --> 00:39:38.459
[man shouting in Mongolian]

00:39:48.344 --> 00:39:50.055
[Jingim]
He was given an honorable death.

00:39:51.056 --> 00:39:55.351
Rolled up in a carpet so that
Tengri the Sky God did not see his blood.

00:39:59.564 --> 00:40:01.983
You will be riding into
battle with us, I hear...

00:40:02.067 --> 00:40:04.485
to give your accounts.

00:40:17.665 --> 00:40:21.002
[Mei Lin] I love you so much.
I have to go.

00:40:21.086 --> 00:40:22.837
But I will see you very soon.

00:40:22.921 --> 00:40:24.505
-[Ling Ling sobbing]
-I love you.

00:40:37.518 --> 00:40:39.729
[Ling Ling crying]

00:41:27.068 --> 00:41:28.778
[sighs deeply]

00:42:26.961 --> 00:42:28.963
[Kublai] Send for Ariq.

00:42:30.173 --> 00:42:34.260
Put up a <i>ger.</i>
Light a fire.

00:43:05.583 --> 00:43:06.751
[scoffs]

00:43:12.798 --> 00:43:13.883
[chuckles]

00:43:15.009 --> 00:43:16.969
Do you remember, older brother...

00:43:17.052 --> 00:43:19.764
the summer
you chased a deer for six days?

00:43:19.847 --> 00:43:23.351
You were gone so long,
our mother thought the wolves got you.

00:43:23.434 --> 00:43:26.354
She made me grind borts
with the women for six more days.

00:43:26.437 --> 00:43:27.438
[Ariq laughs]

00:43:28.523 --> 00:43:31.192
Our father woke up drunk and said,

00:43:31.276 --> 00:43:34.237
"Kublai, why are you
grinding borts like a girl,

00:43:34.320 --> 00:43:36.781
when you should be
out hunting deer?"

00:43:39.033 --> 00:43:40.410
Sorkaktani...

00:43:41.952 --> 00:43:43.413
she was a fine mother.

00:43:45.623 --> 00:43:48.834
A great mother.
Queen of Mongolia.

00:43:54.840 --> 00:43:58.344
It was she who taught us
the code of Grandfather Genghis, yes?

00:43:58.428 --> 00:44:00.805
It was she that taught us
that a true ruler

00:44:00.888 --> 00:44:04.142
must not lose the loyalty
of his allies and subjects.

00:44:05.143 --> 00:44:09.897
The Chinese... Saracen...
Christian or Hindi.

00:44:10.731 --> 00:44:14.235
A wise leader
allows his people their ways.

00:44:14.319 --> 00:44:15.445
[Ariq] Our father...

00:44:15.528 --> 00:44:18.489
son of Genghis,
did not agree with such open gates.

00:44:18.573 --> 00:44:21.951
He drank himself to death.
Behind closed doors.

00:44:24.495 --> 00:44:27.623
Do you know where I was
those six days?

00:44:27.707 --> 00:44:29.792
When you were chasing that deer?

00:44:31.211 --> 00:44:32.837
Making my arrows sharp

00:44:32.920 --> 00:44:36.716
to go after the wolf
and save my brother.

00:44:36.799 --> 00:44:39.009
I was four years old.

00:44:39.719 --> 00:44:42.222
When our brother, Mongke, died...

00:44:42.305 --> 00:44:45.350
Mongolia elected me Khan of Khans.

00:44:45.433 --> 00:44:50.480
Not all of Mongolia, brother.
Not the Princes of the Golden Horde.

00:44:50.563 --> 00:44:53.899
-Not the Chagataid of Persia.
-That is rebellion.

00:44:59.071 --> 00:45:01.073
We can argue that all night.

00:45:02.367 --> 00:45:04.452
I do not want to be
Emperor of China.

00:45:05.411 --> 00:45:08.873
I do not want to be
Ruler of the Face of the Earth.

00:45:08.956 --> 00:45:11.376
I want to be Khan of Mongolia.

00:45:11.459 --> 00:45:13.586
They are one and the same, brother.

00:45:15.505 --> 00:45:18.508
So... it has come to this?

00:45:19.300 --> 00:45:22.177
Not by my choosing.

00:45:24.597 --> 00:45:25.765
The way I see it,

00:45:25.848 --> 00:45:28.726
it is your warriors
setting camp on my land.

00:45:29.935 --> 00:45:31.896
It's because of that point of view...

00:45:31.979 --> 00:45:35.149
my warriors set camp on my land.

00:45:53.959 --> 00:45:56.086
I bid you a good night's rest.

00:45:57.922 --> 00:46:00.841
I'll see you at sunrise.

00:46:29.036 --> 00:46:30.330
[sharpening sword]

00:46:49.264 --> 00:46:53.519
Where do you think
the Venetian merchant is this evening?

00:46:56.522 --> 00:46:58.858
India? Tabriz?

00:47:01.944 --> 00:47:05.322
On my Silk Road, chasing riches.

00:47:07.825 --> 00:47:10.411
I was just about your age when I knew.

00:47:12.455 --> 00:47:14.374
Knew what, Sire?

00:47:14.457 --> 00:47:18.293
That I had to become the man
I wished my father was.

00:47:23.173 --> 00:47:24.592
Tomorrow...

00:47:25.801 --> 00:47:28.095
watch and remember what you see.

00:47:30.890 --> 00:47:32.307
Faithfully.

00:47:43.486 --> 00:47:46.155
[drums playing]

00:48:30.950 --> 00:48:32.326
[drums stop playing]

00:49:16.746 --> 00:49:18.247
Tell me.

00:49:19.540 --> 00:49:25.004
All the way to the horizon.
A sea of men and horses.

00:49:25.087 --> 00:49:27.715
Ready to break ashore.

00:49:29.008 --> 00:49:32.094
The Khan has moved
from his guard to the front.

00:49:34.889 --> 00:49:35.890
Yes.

00:50:38.035 --> 00:50:39.829
[urges horse]

00:50:43.874 --> 00:50:45.334
What is he doing now?

00:50:46.794 --> 00:50:48.295
[Marco] He is riding down.

00:50:49.463 --> 00:50:50.715
Alone.

00:50:50.798 --> 00:50:53.092
This is Mongol against Mongol.

00:50:53.175 --> 00:50:55.135
And only one can win.

00:50:57.054 --> 00:50:58.973
You best pray that it is our side.

00:50:59.056 --> 00:51:00.641
[Ariq scoffing]

00:51:00.725 --> 00:51:02.017
For if we lose...

00:51:02.101 --> 00:51:04.228
Cambulac will be
burned to the ground...

00:51:04.311 --> 00:51:07.189
and we will be made into kindling.

00:51:09.441 --> 00:51:10.943
[urging horse]

00:51:14.196 --> 00:51:15.280
[falcon screeching]

00:51:36.927 --> 00:51:39.096
Look where it has ended, brother.

00:51:40.305 --> 00:51:42.683
You want Mongolia...

00:51:42.767 --> 00:51:44.309
you come and take it.

00:51:45.978 --> 00:51:47.312
[Ariq] It is...

00:51:48.230 --> 00:51:49.649
as it should be.

00:52:45.830 --> 00:52:47.331
[yelling]

00:52:53.295 --> 00:52:54.880
[both grunting]

00:53:48.058 --> 00:53:49.559
[Kublai breathing heavily]

00:54:01.947 --> 00:54:03.157
[yelling in pain]

00:54:07.828 --> 00:54:08.871
[yelling]

00:54:57.127 --> 00:54:58.337
[falcon screeching]

00:55:19.274 --> 00:55:21.151
Men of Karakorum!

00:55:22.194 --> 00:55:23.737
It is over!

00:55:23.820 --> 00:55:25.030
This fight...

00:55:25.114 --> 00:55:29.201
between Mongols is done!

00:55:30.744 --> 00:55:32.454
We stand together now!

00:55:33.455 --> 00:55:35.165
We ride together!

00:55:37.209 --> 00:55:40.379
Every corner of the land
beneath this Blue Sky,

00:55:40.462 --> 00:55:43.215
is ours for the taking!

00:55:44.299 --> 00:55:46.551
Go back to Karakorum.

00:55:46.635 --> 00:55:49.054
Prepare for war!

00:55:49.972 --> 00:55:54.143
For soon,
we ride toward the south.

00:55:55.936 --> 00:55:57.646
[man shouting in foreign language]

00:56:30.637 --> 00:56:32.639
[theme music playing]